Draw: no anti-aliasing passes while navigating on Mesa's v3d (Raspberry Pi)

On a Raspberry Pi 4 (V3D 4.2) every full-screen pass of the viewport costs 3-5 ms at 1322x762, and the
viewport is GPU-bound: orbiting the default cube takes 193 ms per frame. Two of its passes are
anti-aliasing: Workbench's SMAA (Preferences > Viewport > Anti-Aliasing, while navigating) and the
overlays' smooth-wire resolve (Smooth Wires); each costs about 35 ms of the frame (measured with them
switched off, docs/design/blender.md 7.17 in haiku-rpi).

While navigating (RV3D_NAVIGATING / RV3D_PAINTING) on v3d, leave both out: Workbench draws with 0
samples, as with Anti-Aliasing "None", and the overlays draw their wires without the smooth-wire
resolve, as with Smooth Wires off. The first frame after the navigation is anti-aliased as before
(Workbench's TAA then accumulates as usual). Orbiting the default cube by middle-mouse drag: 193 ->
127 ms per frame (5.2 -> 7.9 fps); Material Preview 197 -> 165 ms (only the overlays' part applies).

diff --git a/source/blender/draw/engines/overlay/overlay_antialiasing.cc b/source/blender/draw/engines/overlay/overlay_antialiasing.cc
index 2eefdce..cebe63a 100644
